<p><strong>Somerville's housing reality:</strong></p>

<p><strong>The farmhouse factor:</strong> A lot of Somerville properties are older — homes that have been in families for generations, some with additions built over decades, rooflines that weren't designed with modern gutter systems in mind. We see original sectional gutters held up by hope and habit, fascia boards that should have been replaced 20 years ago, and creative DIY repairs that deserve points for effort.</p>

<p><strong>Rural lot challenges:</strong> Larger lots mean more trees. More trees mean more debris. Without gutter guards, you're cleaning constantly or watching gutters overflow. Properties with acreage also deal with drainage patterns that don't follow nice suburban rules — water flows where gravity takes it, and sometimes that's toward your foundation.</p>

<p><strong>The contractor gap:</strong> Small towns often struggle to get quality contractors. Too far from the city, too small a market, not worth the drive. That's not how we operate. Somerville has been part of our service area since we started. Population 700 doesn't mean you don't deserve quality service.</p>
